<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Laurion</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Laurium</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Laurion is a district at the southern tip of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attica">Attica</a>, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a>, whose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> and lead mines were the main source of Athenian wealth in the classical period. A rich new vein discovered in 483 BCE paid, on the proposal of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/themistocles">Themistocles</a>, for the fleet that won at Salamis. The mines were worked largely by slaves, and the modern town of Lavrio stands nearby.</p></div>
